{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'mechanism draws findings|Small first' ../../../AGENTS.md; rg -n 'Round 33|def (readings_complete|quoted|check_p_row|gain_credit|pair_credit|pilot_decision|main)' PAID-BUILD.md verdict.py; nl -ba PAID-BUILD.md | tail -43; nl -ba e2e-checks.log | tail -47\"","aggregated_output":"85:- When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings: propose one structural rule.\n354:- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\nPAID-BUILD.md:126:## Round 33 findings and the changes (`codex-r33.md`, NOT READY: two)\nverdict.py:50:def readings_complete(fields, key_field, allowed):\nverdict.py:62:def quoted(excerpt, *texts):\nverdict.py:67:def check_p_row(row):\nverdict.py:296:def gain_credit(gain_rows, gain_dates, segment_ends):\nverdict.py:333:def gain_credit(gain_rows, gain_dates, segment_ends, company_ends=None):\nverdict.py:380:def pair_credit(p_read, key, n, linked, control, gain_rows, window):\nverdict.py:411:def pilot_decision(out, p_path, h4_path, gains_path, key_path, allow_dry=False):\nverdict.py:469:def main(out, p_path, h_path, gains_path, key_path):\n    94\t\n    95\t## Rounds 30–31 and the pilot path\n    96\t- Round 30 (NOT READY): H3's selector misses cases; review records not validated (a material failure without its reliance finding;\n    97\t  duplicate rows; a quantified CPU correction stored once per company judgement); completion inferred from replay returning; reading\n    98\t  estimate 18–30 reviewer-hours. Round 31 (reflection, consensus, D708): pilot first, under the rule written in PAID-DESIGN.md §8.\n    99\t- Fixed for the pilot: the gate checks the completed calendar against the pinned one (`planned_days`, fixed apart from the replay's\n   100\t  window; mutant `window cut short` caught, `paid-mutant-7.log`); `verdict.bind_p` refuses a P reading that is not exactly the stores'\n   101\t  pairs (a substituted judgement, a shifted span, a missing or duplicated row); `gain_credit` refuses a material failure without its\n   102\t  reliance finding and a duplicated review, and applies a quantified CPU correction as a corrected range compared on each gain date with\n   103\t  that date's segment range as read; `verdict.pilot_decision` reads pair 1 alone and cannot give the comparison's pass.\n   104\t- Evidence: the six dry sequences rerun with the current harness, all accepted with the calendar check (`paid-dry-*.log`);\n   105\t  `e2e-checks.log`: the full path's 14 checks and the pilot's 7 (a complete reading continues; never a pass; a substituted P judgement and\n   106\t  a missing H4 reading refused; an H4 double count stops; a quantified correction turning the gains definite stops as not improved; every\n   107\t  unquantifiable CPU gain unresolved together stops as undecided).\n   108\t- Still open for the full reading (not the pilot): H3's selector (round 30's cases), H5's duplicate counting.\n   109\t\n   110\t## Round 32 findings and the changes (`codex-r32.md`, NOT READY: three)\n   111\t1. **Readings bound to the regenerated rows:** `bind_p` compares each P row's dates and both answers' full forecast and reasons with the\n   112\t   stores' row; `bind_rows` compares each H4 row (request, read judgements shown and their trace, the CPU judgement, control-1's answer\n   113\t   in force) and each gain row (request, forecast, gain dates) with rows regenerated from the stores; every reading carries its record\n   114\t   (first and second readers, a third when they differ, the final value theirs or the third's) and its excerpt. The official pilot\n   115\t   decision refuses dry summaries (`allow_dry` for the $0 checks only).\n   116\t2. **Numbers validated:** a resolved P class needs finite, ordered ranges for both answers and their excerpts, and must be the class the\n   117\t   ranges give; a quantified CPU correction needs a finite, ordered corrected range; a corrected company answer carried across two gain\n   118\t   dates gives a class per date.\n   119\t3. **Order:** linked double refusal; validity; coverage; harm; control floor; credited P.\n   120\tEvidence: `e2e-checks.log`, 30 checks, exit 0 (the new: dry summaries refused for the official decision; a P row with its forecast text\n   121\tremoved, a class the ranges contradict, a P row without its second reading, an H4 row with another request, an H4 row without the control\n   122\tanswer, and a NaN corrected range refused; coverage short before an H4 double count gives inconclusive; the carried correction gives\n   123\tclear on one date and definite on the other). One fixture of mine set only the final H4 finding, which the new record rule refused; the\n   124\tfixture was completed.\n   125\t\n   126\t## Round 33 findings and the changes (`codex-r33.md`, NOT READY: two)\n   127\t1. **Reading records checked, not only present:** each reader's value must be one of the allowed values; when the first and second\n   128\t   differ, the third must be allowed and carry its quoted source (`third source`); every excerpt (P ranges, H findings) must be a piece of\n   129\t   the answer or request it was read from; every gain review quotes its rule-B trace from the answer. The same record rule now applies to\n   130\t   the full reading's H rows.\n   131\t2. **The CPU correction only on the total-revenue answer:** a CPU increment reviewed on any other answer is refused; a quantified one\n   132\t   needs the increment removed (positive) and a corrected range equal to the company's read range minus it (within $0.05B), and the same\n   133\t   company answer must be read with one range wherever it appears.\n   134\tEvidence: `e2e-checks.log`, 35 checks, exit 0 (new: readings outside the allowed values, an excerpt not from its answer, a gain review\n   135\twithout its trace, a CPU correction on the Data Center answer, and a correction that raises the total are each refused). Two of my\n   136\tfixtures set only a final H finding, which the record rule refused; they were completed.\n   519\t  \"readable\": {\n   520\t   \"linked\": 58,\n   521\t   \"control\": 73\n   522\t  }\n   523\t }\n   524\t}\n   525\t{\"gain review rows\": 6}\n   526\t{\"gain review rows\": 6}\n   527\t{\"gain review rows\": 6}\n   528\t{\n   529\t \"a complete synthetic reading passes\": true,\n   530\t \"P rows only (no H review) is refused\": true,\n   531\t \"an unread H row is refused\": true,\n   532\t \"an incomplete gain review is refused\": true,\n   533\t \"every gain withdrawn by its reviews: not improved, fail\": true,\n   534\t \"an H4 double count fails\": true,\n   535\t \"a linked grounding error the control lacks fails\": true,\n   536\t \"two more H5 failures in a linked sequence fail\": true,\n   537\t \"a sequence the gate rejected makes it inconclusive\": true,\n   538\t \"a linked double refusal fails even with no P rows\": true,\n   539\t \"four more linked refusals on matched reader-days fail (H1)\": true,\n   540\t \"three more are tolerated (H1)\": true,\n   541\t \"a material failure without a reliance finding is refused\": true,\n   542\t \"a substituted P judgement is refused\": true,\n   543\t \"pilot: a complete reading of an improved pair continues\": true,\n   544\t \"pilot: never gives the comparison's pass\": true,\n   545\t \"pilot: a substituted P judgement is refused\": true,\n   546\t \"pilot: a missing H4 reading is refused\": true,\n   547\t \"pilot: an H4 double count stops\": true,\n   548\t \"pilot: a quantified CPU correction is applied per gain date (the gains become definite: stop)\": true,\n   549\t \"pilot: every unquantifiable CPU gain unresolved together (stop: undecided)\": true,\n   550\t \"pilot: the official decision refuses dry summaries\": true,\n   551\t \"pilot: a P row with its forecast text removed is refused\": true,\n   552\t \"pilot: a class the ranges contradict is refused\": true,\n   553\t \"pilot: a P row without the second reading is refused\": true,\n   554\t \"pilot: an H4 row with another request is refused\": true,\n   555\t \"pilot: an H4 row without the control answer is refused\": true,\n   556\t \"pilot: a NaN corrected range is refused\": true,\n   557\t \"pilot: coverage short comes before harm (inconclusive)\": true,\n   558\t \"credit: a carried corrected answer gives a class per date\": true,\n   559\t \"pilot: readings outside the allowed values are refused\": true,\n   560\t \"pilot: an excerpt not from its answer is refused\": true,\n   561\t \"pilot: a gain review without its rule-B trace is refused\": true,\n   562\t \"pilot: a CPU correction on the Data Center answer is refused\": true,\n   563\t \"pilot: a correction that raises the total is refused\": true\n   564\t}\n   565\texit 0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba verdict.py | sed -n '469,531p'; nl -ba e2e_checks.py | sed -n '49,59p;145,195p;216,259p'; nl -ba PAID-DESIGN.md | sed -n '93,102p;141,154p'; ls -ld /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/{paid-dry3,e2e/pilot}\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba verdict.py | sed -n '469,531p'; nl -ba e2e_checks.py | sed -n '49,59p;145,195p;216,259p'; nl -ba PAID-DESIGN.md | sed -n '93,102p;141,154p'; ls -ld /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/{paid-dry3,e2e/pilot}\"","aggregated_output":"   469\tdef main(out, p_path, h_path, gains_path, key_path):\n   470\t    import worksheet\n   471\t    summaries = {name: json.loads((Path(out) / name / 'summary.json').read_text()) for name in SEQUENCES}\n   472\t    flags = summary_flags(out)\n   473\t    if flags['linked_double_refusal']:                          # precedence (1), before any worksheet is required\n   474\t        print(json.dumps({'verdict': ('fail', 'a linked double refusal')}))\n   475\t        return 'fail', 'a linked double refusal'\n   476\t    if flags['infrastructure_stop'] or flags['control_double_refusal'] or flags['trajectory_difference'] or \\\n   477\t            not all(s['acceptance']['accepted'] for s in summaries.values()):\n   478\t        print(json.dumps({'verdict': ('inconclusive', 'invalid or incomplete'), 'flags': flags,\n   479\t                          'rejected': [n for n, s in summaries.items() if not s['acceptance']['accepted']]}))\n   480\t        return 'inconclusive', 'invalid or incomplete'\n   481\t    key = json.loads(Path(key_path).read_text())\n   482\t    p_read = json.loads(Path(p_path).read_text())\n   483\t    bind_p(p_read, key, out)\n   484\t    classes = read_classes(p_read, key)\n   485\t    h_rows = json.loads(Path(h_path).read_text())\n   486\t    expected = {h_key(r) for name in SEQUENCES for r in worksheet.h_rows(out, name, None)}\n   487\t    read = {h_key(r): r for r in h_rows}\n   488\t    if set(read) != expected:\n   489\t        raise Refused(f'the H packet holds {len(set(read) & expected)} of the {len(expected)} expected rows '\n   490\t                      f'({len(set(read) - expected)} unexpected)')\n   491\t    for k, row in read.items():\n   492\t        if row['reader']['finding'] not in H_FINDINGS[row['part']] or not readings_complete(row['reader'], 'finding', H_FINDINGS[row['part']]) or \\\n   493\t                not quoted(row['reader'].get('excerpt'), row.get('forecast'), row.get('reasons'), row.get('reference'), row.get('request')):\n   494\t            raise Refused(f'{k}: the finding, its reading record or its quoted excerpt is missing')\n   495\t        if row['part'] == 'H3' and row['reader']['finding'] == 'grounding error' and row['reader']['error type'] not in ERROR_TYPES:\n   496\t            raise Refused(f'{k}: a grounding error needs its type, one of {ERROR_TYPES}')\n   497\t    derived, _ = h_flags(h_rows)\n   498\t    flags.update(derived)\n   499\t    flags['h1'] = any(h1(summaries).values())\n   500\t    gain_rows = json.loads(Path(gains_path).read_text())\n   501\t    window = calendar()\n   502\t    outcomes, details = [], {}\n   503\t    for n in ('1', '2', '3'):\n   504\t        linked, control = classes[f'linked-{n}'], classes[f'control-{n}']\n   505\t        provisional = pair_outcome(linked, control, {}, window)[0]\n   506\t        credit = {}\n   507\t        if provisional == 'improved':\n   508\t            credit = pair_credit(p_read, key, n, linked, control, gain_rows, window)\n   509\t        outcome, detail = pair_outcome(linked, control, credit, window)\n   510\t        outcomes.append(outcome)\n   511\t        details[n] = dict(detail, outcome=outcome, provisional=provisional, adjusted=credit)\n   512\t    result = verdict(outcomes, flags)\n   513\t    print(json.dumps({'pairs': details, 'flags': flags, 'verdict': result}, indent=1))\n   514\t    return result\n   515\t\n   516\t\n   517\t# ---------- the $0 verdict checks ----------\n   518\t\n   519\tdef synthetic(definite_control=(), definite_linked=(), unresolved_linked=(), total=WINDOW_DATES):\n   520\t    dates = [f'd{i:02d}' for i in range(total)]\n   521\t    control = {d: ('definite' if d in definite_control else 'clear') for d in dates}\n   522\t    linked = {d: ('definite' if d in definite_linked else 'unresolved' if d in unresolved_linked else 'clear') for d in dates}\n   523\t    return dates, linked, control\n   524\t\n   525\t\n   526\tdef checks():\n   527\t    results = {}\n   528\t    dates, linked, control = synthetic(definite_control=('d01', 'd02'))\n   529\t    results['control 2 definite, linked none: improved'] = pair_outcome(linked, control, {}, dates)[0] == 'improved'\n   530\t    results['round 25: both gains reviewed and withdrawn: a tie, not improved'] = \\\n   531\t        pair_outcome(linked, control, {'d01': 'none', 'd02': 'none'}, dates)[0] == 'not improved'\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef mark(row, value, segment=None):\n    52\t    \"\"\"A P reading with its record: both readers agree; ranges and excerpts consistent with the class.\"\"\"\n    53\t    s = segment if segment is not None else (420.0 if value == 'definite' else 380.0)\n    54\t    row['reader'].update({'class': value, 'first class': value, 'second class': value, 'segment low': s, 'segment high': s,\n    55\t                          'company low': 400.0, 'company high': 400.0, 'segment excerpt': row['segment forecast'][:9],\n    56\t                          'company excerpt': row['company forecast'][:9]})\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\tdef write(folder, p, h, gains):\n   145\t    p, h4 = worksheet.build_pilot(out, str(folder / 'packet'), str(key_path), seed=3)\n   146\t    key = json.loads(key_path.read_text())\n   147\t    p, h4 = copy.deepcopy(p), copy.deepcopy(h4)\n   148\t    by = {}\n   149\t    for row in p:\n   150\t        by.setdefault(key[row['sequence']], []).append(row)\n   151\t    for name, rows in by.items():\n   152\t        rows.sort(key=lambda r: r['dates'][0])\n   153\t        for i, row in enumerate(rows):\n   154\t            mark(row, 'definite' if name == 'control-1' and i < 3 else 'clear')\n   155\t    for row in h4:\n   156\t        row['reader'].update({'finding': 'ok', 'first finding': 'ok', 'second finding': 'ok', 'excerpt': row['forecast'][:9]})\n   157\t    (folder / 'p-read.json').write_text(json.dumps(p))\n   158\t    gains = worksheet.gains(out, str(folder / 'p-read.json'), str(key_path), str(folder / 'gains.json'))\n   159\t    for g in gains:\n   160\t        g['reader'].update({'rule B material failure': False, 'cpu increment': 'none', 'rule B trace': g['forecast'][:9]})\n   161\t\n   162\t    def decide(p_, h4_, gains_):\n   163\t        for name, data in (('p.json', p_), ('h4.json', h4_), ('g.json', gains_)):\n   164\t            (folder / name).write_text(json.dumps(data))\n   165\t        try:\n   166\t            return verdict.pilot_decision(out, str(folder / 'p.json'), str(folder / 'h4.json'), str(folder / 'g.json'), str(key_path), allow_dry=True)\n   167\t        except verdict.Refused as error:\n   168\t            return ('refused', str(error)[:100])\n   169\t    results = {'pilot: a complete reading of an improved pair continues': decide(p, h4, gains)[0] == 'continue'}\n   170\t    results['pilot: never gives the comparison\\'s pass'] = 'pass' not in {decide(p, h4, gains)[0]}\n   171\t    sub = copy.deepcopy(p)\n   172\t    sub[0]['company judgement'] += 100000\n   173\t    results['pilot: a substituted P judgement is refused'] = decide(sub, h4, gains)[0] == 'refused'\n   174\t    results['pilot: a missing H4 reading is refused'] = decide(p, h4[1:], gains)[0] == 'refused'\n   175\t    double = copy.deepcopy(h4)\n   176\t    double[0]['reader'].update({'finding': 'double count', 'first finding': 'double count', 'second finding': 'double count'})\n   177\t    results['pilot: an H4 double count stops'] = decide(p, double, gains) == ('stop', 'confirmed harm (H4 double count)')\n   178\t    corrected = copy.deepcopy(gains)\n   179\t    for g in corrected:\n   180\t        if g['view'] == 'v14':\n   181\t            g['reader'].update({'cpu increment': 'quantified', 'increment removed': 30.0, 'corrected low': 370.0,\n   182\t                                'corrected high': 370.0})                       # $400B less $30B, below the linked segment's 380\n   183\t    results['pilot: a quantified CPU correction is applied per gain date (the gains become definite: stop)'] = \\\n   184\t        decide(p, h4, corrected) == ('stop', 'pair 1 not improved')\n   185\t    unquantified = copy.deepcopy(gains)\n   186\t    for g in unquantified:\n   187\t        if g['view'] == 'v14':\n   188\t            g['reader']['cpu increment'] = 'unquantifiable'\n   189\t    results['pilot: every unquantifiable CPU gain unresolved together (stop: undecided)'] = decide(p, h4, unquantified) == ('stop', 'pair 1 undecided')\n   190\t    try:\n   191\t        verdict.pilot_decision(out, str(folder / 'p.json'), str(folder / 'h4.json'), str(folder / 'g.json'), str(key_path))\n   192\t        results['pilot: the official decision refuses dry summaries'] = False\n   193\t    except verdict.Refused:\n   194\t        results['pilot: the official decision refuses dry summaries'] = True\n   195\t    no_text = copy.deepcopy(p)\n   216\t    short = copy.deepcopy(p)\n   217\t    for row in [r for r in short if key[r['sequence']] == 'linked-1'][:15]:\n   218\t        mark(row, 'unresolved')\n   219\t        row['reader'].update({k: None for k in ('segment low', 'segment high', 'company low', 'company high')})\n   220\t    short_double = copy.deepcopy(h4)\n   221\t    short_double[0]['reader'].update({'finding': 'double count', 'first finding': 'double count', 'second finding': 'double count'})\n   222\t    results['pilot: coverage short comes before harm (inconclusive)'] = decide(short, short_double, gains) == ('inconclusive', 'coverage short')\n   223\t    # one corrected company answer carried across two gain dates: the segment below it on one date, above it on the other\n   224\t    rows = [{'judgement': 1, 'view': 'v14', 'forecast': 'about $405B', 'reader': {'rule B material failure': False, 'cpu increment': 'quantified',\n   225\t                                                                                  'increment removed': 30.0, 'corrected low': 375.0,\n   226\t                                                                                  'corrected high': 375.0, 'rule B trace': '$405B'}},\n   227\t            {'judgement': 2, 'view': 'v9', 'forecast': 'about $360B', 'reader': {'rule B material failure': False, 'cpu increment': 'none', 'rule B trace': '$360B'}},\n   228\t            {'judgement': 3, 'view': 'v9', 'forecast': 'about $390B', 'reader': {'rule B material failure': False, 'cpu increment': 'none', 'rule B trace': '$390B'}}]\n   229\t    credit = verdict.gain_credit(rows, {'d1': (2, 1), 'd2': (3, 1)}, {'d1': (360.0, 360.0), 'd2': (390.0, 390.0)}, {1: (405.0, 405.0)})\n   230\t    results['credit: a carried corrected answer gives a class per date'] = credit == {'d1': 'clear', 'd2': 'definite'}\n   231\t    bad_values = copy.deepcopy(p)\n   232\t    bad_values[0]['reader'].update({'first class': False, 'second class': 7, 'third class': bad_values[0]['reader']['class'], 'third source': 'x'})\n   233\t    results['pilot: readings outside the allowed values are refused'] = decide(bad_values, h4, gains)[0] == 'refused'\n   234\t    made_up = copy.deepcopy(p)\n   235\t    made_up[0]['reader']['segment excerpt'] = 'a sentence that is not in the answer'\n   236\t    results['pilot: an excerpt not from its answer is refused'] = decide(made_up, h4, gains)[0] == 'refused'\n   237\t    no_trace = copy.deepcopy(gains)\n   238\t    no_trace[0]['reader']['rule B trace'] = ''\n   239\t    results['pilot: a gain review without its rule-B trace is refused'] = decide(p, h4, no_trace)[0] == 'refused'\n   240\t    on_segment = copy.deepcopy(gains)\n   241\t    for g in on_segment:\n   242\t        if g['view'] == 'v9':\n   243\t            g['reader'].update({'cpu increment': 'quantified', 'increment removed': 10.0, 'corrected low': 390.0, 'corrected high': 390.0})\n   244\t    results['pilot: a CPU correction on the Data Center answer is refused'] = decide(p, h4, on_segment)[0] == 'refused'\n   245\t    raised = copy.deepcopy(gains)\n   246\t    for g in raised:\n   247\t        if g['view'] == 'v14':\n   248\t            g['reader'].update({'cpu increment': 'quantified', 'increment removed': -10.0, 'corrected low': 410.0, 'corrected high': 410.0})\n   249\t    results['pilot: a correction that raises the total is refused'] = decide(p, h4, raised)[0] == 'refused'\n   250\t    return results\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   254\t    sys.exit(0 if main(sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]) else 1)\n    93\t- **Credit (rounds 24–25; one rule):** a **gain** is a date on which the linked arm is not definite and the control is definite. Only\n    94\t  gains are ever adjusted; no other date's class changes for credit. When a pair is provisionally improved, **every** gain is reviewed:\n    95\t  both linked answers in force on it (v9's and v14's), deduplicated by judgement id, are read for July's rule B (arithmetic following\n    96\t  from stated inputs; each assumption that sizes the result disclosed and supported) and for H4. A gain whose forecasts carry a material\n    97\t  rule-B failure on which its reconciliation rests earns no credit (counted definite for P). A gain resting on an unsupported CPU\n    98\t  increment: when the increment can be quantified, the forecast with it removed gives the gain's credit-adjusted class; when it cannot,\n    99\t  the gain counts unresolved: **every** such gain of the pair is marked unresolved, and the bounds are then recomputed once across the\n   100\t  pair (round 26: two gains marked one at a time could each look harmless). Each date keeps its actual class in the report beside its\n   101\t  credit-adjusted class; P is recomputed on the credit-adjusted classes. A confirmed CPU double count stays a harm (H4) whatever its\n   102\t  date.\n   141\t**The worksheet (pinned before the launch; rounds 24, 28, 29):** built by `worksheet.py` from the six stores and archives after the run,\n   142\tits format and code reviewed and run on the dry outputs before the send, in **two packets**: the P packet (blind: shuffled labels, no\n   143\tarm name, P rows only) for the blind reader, and the H packet (H3, H4, H5 rows, which reveal the arm through their requests); the gain\n   144\tpacket follows the P reading. `verdict.py` takes the read packets themselves: it refuses unless every expected H row (regenerated from\n   145\tthe stores) carries a valid final finding, derives H1 from the dated judge rows of the six summaries, H3–H5 from the read rows, and each\n   146\tgain's credit from the reviews of its two supplying answers; it requires all six summaries accepted by the gate, and a linked double\n   147\trefusal fails before any packet is required. One P row per distinct v9/v14 answer pair per sequence, keyed by\n   148\tboth judgement ids and the pair's date span; it carries both answers' full `implied_outcome` and reasons, and fields for the reader:\n   149\tthe FY2027 low and high ends as each answer finally states them, the excerpt they come from, the class, a note. H3, H4 and H5 rows carry\n   150\tthe exact request text (dependency block marked), the read judgement each figure came through, and the dated source quotes. Worked\n   151\texample (old-1 09-08): Data Center \"$419 billion for FY2027\" against total revenue \"$414.3 billion ... supports roughly $414–421\n   152\tbillion\": low end 419 is not above high end 421, so **overlap**, though the parser took $414.3B and flagged it definite. Claude reads\n   153\tfirst; a blind reader (Codex, labels shuffled, key kept outside the repository) second; every disagreement that could change a pair's\n   154\toutcome, an H3 or H4 finding, or an H5 mark goes to a third, source-backed read whose class decides. Reading load on old-2's schedule:\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 10 lchingen  wheel  320 Nov 21 13:13 /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/e2e/pilot\ndrwxr-xr-x@  8 lchingen  wheel  256 Nov 21 12:58 /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-dry3\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport contextlib,copy,io,json,tempfile\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nimport verdict\nfrom collections import Counter\nbase=Path(\\\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad\\\")\nout=base/\\\"paid-dry3\\\"\nfolder=base/\\\"e2e\\\"/\\\"pilot\\\"\np,h,g,k=[json.loads((folder/f).read_text()) for f in (\\\"p-read.json\\\",\\\"h4.json\\\",\\\"g.json\\\",\\\"key.json\\\")]\nfor r in h:\n    r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"first finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"second finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"third finding\\\":None})\nfor r in g:\n    r[\\\"reader\\\"]={\\\"rule B material failure\\\":False,\\\"cpu increment\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"rule B trace\\\":r[\\\"forecast\\\"][:9]}\ndef decide(label, p,h,g):\n    mem={\\\"/INPUT/P\\\":p,\\\"/INPUT/H\\\":h,\\\"/INPUT/G\\\":g,\\\"/KEY\\\":k}\n    read_orig=Path.read_text\n    def read(self,*a,**kw):\n        if str(self) in mem: return json.dumps(mem[str(self)])\n        return read_orig(self,*a,**kw)\n    def write(self,s,*a,**kw):\n        assert str(self).startswith(\\\"/MEM/\\\")\n        mem[str(self)]=json.loads(s)\n    with patch.object(Path,\\\"read_text\\\",read),patch.object(Path,\\\"write_text\\\",write),patch.object(tempfile,\\\"TemporaryDirectory\\\",lambda:contextlib.nullcontext(\\\"/MEM\\\")),contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()):\n        try: result=verdict.pilot_decision(out,\\\"/INPUT/P\\\",\\\"/INPUT/H\\\",\\\"/INPUT/G\\\",\\\"/KEY\\\",allow_dry=True)\n        except verdict.Refused as error: result=(\\\"refused\\\",str(error)[:100])\n    print(label, result)\ndecide(\\\"baseline\\\",p,h,g)\npp,hh=copy.deepcopy(p),copy.deepcopy(h)\nr=next(r for r in pp if r[\\\"reader\\\"][\\\"class\\\"]==\\\"clear\\\")\nr[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"first class\\\":\\\"definite\\\",\\\"second class\\\":\\\"clear\\\",\\\"third class\\\":\\\"clear\\\",\\\"third source\\\":True})\nhh[0][\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"first finding\\\":\\\"double count\\\",\\\"second finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"third finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"third source\\\":\\\"   \\\"})\ndecide(\\\"both disagreements settle with no third source\\\",pp,hh,g)\npp=copy.deepcopy(p)\nfor r in pp:\n    if k[r[\\\"sequence\\\"]]==\\\"linked-1\\\":\n        r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"segment low\\\":380.02,\\\"segment high\\\":380.02})\nexact=copy.deepcopy(g)\nfor r in exact:\n    if r[\\\"view\\\"]==\\\"v14\\\":\n        r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"cpu increment\\\":\\\"quantified\\\",\\\"increment removed\\\":20.0,\\\"corrected low\\\":380.0,\\\"corrected high\\\":380.0})\ndecide(\\\"400 less 20 = 380, below 380.02\\\",pp,h,exact)\nfor r in exact:\n    if r[\\\"view\\\"]==\\\"v14\\\":\n        r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"corrected low\\\":380.04,\\\"corrected high\\\":380.04})\ndecide(\\\"400 less 20 reported as 380.04\\\",pp,h,exact)\nfor n in (\\\"linked-1\\\",\\\"control-1\\\"):\n    for question in (\\\"segment judgement\\\",\\\"company judgement\\\"):\n        counter=Counter(r[question] for r in p if k[r[\\\"sequence\\\"]]==n)\n        print(n,question,\\\"repeated\\\",sum(c>1 for c in counter.values()))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport contextlib,copy,io,json,tempfile\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nimport verdict\nfrom collections import Counter\nbase=Path(\\\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad\\\")\nout=base/\\\"paid-dry3\\\"\nfolder=base/\\\"e2e\\\"/\\\"pilot\\\"\np,h,g,k=[json.loads((folder/f).read_text()) for f in (\\\"p-read.json\\\",\\\"h4.json\\\",\\\"g.json\\\",\\\"key.json\\\")]\nfor r in h:\n    r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"first finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"second finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"third finding\\\":None})\nfor r in g:\n    r[\\\"reader\\\"]={\\\"rule B material failure\\\":False,\\\"cpu increment\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"rule B trace\\\":r[\\\"forecast\\\"][:9]}\ndef decide(label, p,h,g):\n    mem={\\\"/INPUT/P\\\":p,\\\"/INPUT/H\\\":h,\\\"/INPUT/G\\\":g,\\\"/KEY\\\":k}\n    read_orig=Path.read_text\n    def read(self,*a,**kw):\n        if str(self) in mem: return json.dumps(mem[str(self)])\n        return read_orig(self,*a,**kw)\n    def write(self,s,*a,**kw):\n        assert str(self).startswith(\\\"/MEM/\\\")\n        mem[str(self)]=json.loads(s)\n    with patch.object(Path,\\\"read_text\\\",read),patch.object(Path,\\\"write_text\\\",write),patch.object(tempfile,\\\"TemporaryDirectory\\\",lambda:contextlib.nullcontext(\\\"/MEM\\\")),contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()):\n        try: result=verdict.pilot_decision(out,\\\"/INPUT/P\\\",\\\"/INPUT/H\\\",\\\"/INPUT/G\\\",\\\"/KEY\\\",allow_dry=True)\n        except verdict.Refused as error: result=(\\\"refused\\\",str(error)[:100])\n    print(label, result)\ndecide(\\\"baseline\\\",p,h,g)\npp,hh=copy.deepcopy(p),copy.deepcopy(h)\nr=next(r for r in pp if r[\\\"reader\\\"][\\\"class\\\"]==\\\"clear\\\")\nr[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"first class\\\":\\\"definite\\\",\\\"second class\\\":\\\"clear\\\",\\\"third class\\\":\\\"clear\\\",\\\"third source\\\":True})\nhh[0][\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"first finding\\\":\\\"double count\\\",\\\"second finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"third finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"third source\\\":\\\"   \\\"})\ndecide(\\\"both disagreements settle with no third source\\\",pp,hh,g)\npp=copy.deepcopy(p)\nfor r in pp:\n    if k[r[\\\"sequence\\\"]]==\\\"linked-1\\\":\n        r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"segment low\\\":380.02,\\\"segment high\\\":380.02})\nexact=copy.deepcopy(g)\nfor r in exact:\n    if r[\\\"view\\\"]==\\\"v14\\\":\n        r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"cpu increment\\\":\\\"quantified\\\",\\\"increment removed\\\":20.0,\\\"corrected low\\\":380.0,\\\"corrected high\\\":380.0})\ndecide(\\\"400 less 20 = 380, below 380.02\\\",pp,h,exact)\nfor r in exact:\n    if r[\\\"view\\\"]==\\\"v14\\\":\n        r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"corrected low\\\":380.04,\\\"corrected high\\\":380.04})\ndecide(\\\"400 less 20 reported as 380.04\\\",pp,h,exact)\nfor n in (\\\"linked-1\\\",\\\"control-1\\\"):\n    for question in (\\\"segment judgement\\\",\\\"company judgement\\\"):\n        counter=Counter(r[question] for r in p if k[r[\\\"sequence\\\"]]==n)\n        print(n,question,\\\"repeated\\\",sum(c>1 for c in counter.values()))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"baseline ('continue', 'pair 1 improved after the gain review, H1 and H4 clear')\nboth disagreements settle with no third source ('continue', 'pair 1 improved after the gain review, H1 and H4 clear')\n400 less 20 = 380, below 380.02 ('stop', 'pair 1 not improved')\n400 less 20 reported as 380.04 ('continue', 'pair 1 improved after the gain review, H1 and H4 clear')\nlinked-1 segment judgement repeated 0\nlinked-1 company judgement repeated 1\ncontrol-1 segment judgement repeated 2\ncontrol-1 company judgement repeated 1\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nimport json\nbase=Path(\\\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/e2e/pilot\\\")\np=json.loads((base/\\\"p-read.json\\\").read_text())\nk=json.loads((base/\\\"key.json\\\").read_text())\nfor spec in (\\\"company judgement\\\",\\\"segment judgement\\\"):\n    rows=defaultdict(list)\n    for r in p:\n        if k[r[\\\"sequence\\\"]]==\\\"control-1\\\": rows[r[spec]].append((r[\\\"dates\\\"],r[\\\"reader\\\"][\\\"class\\\"],r[\\\"segment judgement\\\"],r[\\\"company judgement\\\"]))\n    print(spec,{i:v for i,v in rows.items() if len(v)>1})\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
