e,\"cpu increment\":\"none\",\"rule B trace\":r[\"forecast\"][:9]}\n        mem[\"/G\"]=expected\n        result=verdict.pilot_decision(out,\"/P\",\"/H\",\"/G\",\"/KEY\",allow_dry=True)\n    print(label,result)\ndecide(\"one carried control answer read as both 400 and 370\",p,g)\nfor r in p:\n    if k[r[\"sequence\"]]==\"control-1\" and r[\"company judgement\"]==153:\n        r[\"reader\"].update({\"company low\":400,\"company high\":400,\"class\":\"clear\",\"first class\":\"clear\",\"second class\":\"clear\"})\ndecide(\"one coherent reading of the carried control answer\",p,g)\n'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"one carried control answer read as both 400 and 370 ('continue', 'pair 1 improved after the gain review, H1 and H4 clear')\none coherent reading of the carried control answer ('inconclusive', 'control-1 under 2 definite dates')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The round-33 changes reject invalid reading labels, excerpts absent from the supplied text, missing Rule B quotes, and CPU corrections entered on Data Center’s answer. I still reproduced three ways for the dry pilot to return `continue` without meeting the written rule. [Round-33 checks](e2e-checks.log:559) · [Pilot rule](PAID-DESIGN.md:201)\n\n1. **A disputed reading can be settled without a source.** `readings_complete` checks that `third source` has a truthy value. I supplied `true` for a disputed P reading and spaces for a disputed H4 finding, then used the third finding to clear an H4 double-count disagreement. The pilot continued. Require an actual quote tied to the regenerated evidence for the disputed finding. The full verdict uses the same check and matches its H rows by key, so its quote check should also use regenerated evidence rather than text carried in the submitted row. The gain check now requires a quote, but the dry fixture satisfies it by copying the first nine characters of the forecast. The gain review needs to record how its quoted inputs support the Rule B finding. [Adjudication rule](PAID-DESIGN.md:147) · [Reading validation](verdict.py:50) · [Pilot H4 check](verdict.py:431) · [Full H-row check](verdict.py:485) · [Gain fixture](e2e_checks.py:158)\n\n2. **Rounding can reverse the CPU-credit decision.** With a **$380.02B** segment forecast, removing **$20B** from the **$400B** company forecast gives **$380B**. That stopped the pilot. Entering **$380.04B** as the corrected total passed the tolerance check and made the pilot continue. Calculate the endpoints used for classification directly from the original range and the increment removed. Any tolerance for a reader’s transcription should stay out of the scored comparison. [Credit rule](PAID-DESIGN.md:93) · [Tolerance and classification](verdict.py:360)\n\n3. **The same control answer can supply two different ranges.** The new consistency check runs only for provisionally improved linked sequences. In the dry fixture, I read control company judgement `153` as **$400B on July 18** and **$370B on July 19**. That created the second definite date needed to continue. Reading the carried answer consistently at $400B made the pilot inconclusive. Enforce one resolved range per supplying judgement for both questions in both arms before counting any dates. [P validation](verdict.py:87) · [Range consistency check](verdict.py:380) · [Control floor](PAID-DESIGN.md:83)\n\nAdd these counterexamples to the existing dry checks before asking Alex for the proposed **$2.50** ceiling. [Pilot ceiling](PAID-DESIGN.md:210)"}}
